  "limitations": [
    "Edges are aggregated with the attack label in the grouping key, so these are not deployment-valid estimates.",
    "Classes 3 (dos, 4 edges) and 7 (ransomware, 3 edges) remain in the graph for message passing but are excluded from the metric. A 10-class macro-F1 on this graph is not a reportable number.",
    "The LLM rung (0.2785) sits below the GNN rung: the whitened-prototype scorer collapses under this graph's imbalance (582:1; seven attack classes have <=35 edges).",
    "No rung comparison is statistically separated once training-seed variance is included (two-level bootstrap, 3 seeds). Point-estimate orderings are reported as orderings only.",
    "Training-seed variance is measured; fold-partition variance is NOT (the split is fixed at seed 42). The reported std is a lower bound on total uncertainty.",
    "The real-versus-head_only ablation combines feedback injection and final semantic fusion. Finding 3 (archive 2026-09-06) shows the canonical injected bias was ~0.02-0.08 on unit-variance features, so the loop's edge over head_only is attributable to fusion, not feedback.",
    "The selected top_k_percent and injection_scale were optimized on rotating validation folds; nested cross-validation or an untouched set is required for a fully unbiased final estimate.",
